      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The effects of placebo and proxodolol, a new hybrid (beta-, alpha-) adrenoblocking agent, on exercise tolerance, hemodynamics and the conduction system were compared in 28 patients with coronary heart disease, Functional Class II-III exercise-induced angina pectoris at rest and during bicycle ergometric exercise test. Proxodolol was shown to exert a significant dose-dependent antianginal effect without producing any negative effect on atrioventricular and intraventricular conduction."},
